  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Tall thick blackrock walls extend thousands of li. The city sits on the upper half of Wan Cheng mountain, with rock houses and steel towers lined up toward the peak. On the peak stands a majestic steel tower more than three hundred metres tall with almost a hundred floors, rustic and ancient, with white clouds around it like mist.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sunlight shows carriages, horses, and crowds moving through a prosperous city. The clan leader pavilion stands at the mountain peak, heavily defended, with little ordinary traffic and vigilant patrols of Gu Masters. There Tie Ruo Nan speaks with the sitting Tie Clan leader, her uncle, days after returning from her father’s death.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "upper-half-of-wan-cheng-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
